course: dictionary
lesson: 5333
title: Keystone: the stone that holds it all up
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A keystone is the stone at the very top, in the middle of an arch. It locks the other stones in place, so the whole arch stands up. Take it out and the arch falls down.
explain: The word also means the most important part of a plan or idea, the one that everything else depends on. «The keystone of our plan is teamwork.» Without teamwork, the rest of the plan would fall apart. Ask yourself: is the sentence about stones, or about ideas?
explain: In science, a keystone species is an animal or plant that a whole habitat depends on. «An animal that keeps a whole habitat in balance, like the sea otter, is called a keystone species.» Here keystone describes the species, a bit like the stone in the arch: it holds the rest of the living things together.
fact: A keystone is the central, wedge-shaped stone at the top of an arch that holds the other stones in place.
fact: «Keystone» can also mean the most important part of a plan, idea or system.
fact: A keystone species is an animal or plant that its whole ecosystem depends on, like sea otters or beavers.
fact: Roman bridges and church arches stand up because of their keystone.
fact: Pennsylvania is nicknamed «the Keystone State».
exercise: «Without the keystone, the whole arch would fall down.» What does keystone mean here? | A bright stone found on the beach | The bottom step of a staircase | *The central stone at the top that holds the arch together
exercise: «The keystone of our plan is teamwork.» What does keystone mean here? | A small hole in the wall | Something written in pencil | A pair of door keys | *The most important part, the one everything else depends on
exercise: Sea otters are a keystone species. Which animal is a keystone species? | *A sea otter, which keeps its whole habitat in balance | A pebble on a beach | A cloud drifting over the hills | A tin can left on a path
test: In «keystone species», what kind of word is keystone? | A noun, the name of a thing | *An adjective, describing the kind of species | A verb | A full stop
test: If a keystone species is removed from its ecosystem, what happens? | The species grows twice as big | It moves to a new shelter | Nothing changes for the other living things | *The ecosystem changes greatly
exam: Which sentence uses keystone to mean the most important part of an idea? | Pennsylvania has many farms and forests | The keystone species lives in the sea | The keystone of the old bridge was loose | *The keystone of the argument was fairness
